WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:04.000
One month ago

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.170
There's Hayase's right punch, and Akaboshi stumbles!

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.550
This match will determine who will rise up to the world championships!

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:14.510
Contrary to popular opinion, Hayase is overwhelming Akaboshi!

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.220
And Hayase attacks!

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:20.840
Akaboshi doesn't look like he's doing too good; he's moving sluggishly.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.070
There it is! Hayase's finishing high-rise upper!

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.250
And it's a finish, it's over!

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:46.460
Without even a scratch on him, the worldly-wise Hayase Tsubasa takes his seventh consecutive win!

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:50.590
Hayase-senshu!

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.710
NOTE: <i>Senshu</i> (選手) is an add-on term for sports players.

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:54.710
That was a remarkable K.O. you've done in the last round for the world championships!

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:56.720
Please tell us what your next destination is!

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:02.370
Next, is the world!

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:06.810
Yoshino, look!

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.860
This looks like a case!

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:13.750
What? Horse-racing?

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:14.570
No!

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:15.860
The article over here!

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:22.050
"One More Week Until Hayase Tsubasa Faces His Title Match..."

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:23.090
What's wrong with this?

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:24.490
This Hayase guy...

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:26.360
Smells like a Digimon's involved.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.750
In his previous match, his opponent dropped out of the competition.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.480
Before that, he won by default.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:36.240
And before that, his contender had a cold and wasn't in any condition to fight.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.130
Don't you think this streak is weird?

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.870
It certainly is strange...

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:43.820
But that isn't enough to decide it's a scandal.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.340
No, this is our case! I'm sure of it!

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:50.230
Don't talk as if you know him, Masaru.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.470
What's with you, Tohma?

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:53.700
Raining on my parade?

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:54.890
Yeah!

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:57.440
It's rare for Aniki to find a case!

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:59.070
What d'you mean "rare?!"

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:03.080
That man will never do anything unjust!

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:06.920
Hmph!

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.410
The other thing to consider is that he's way over his prime, at 35!

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:14.900
Yet he's defeating world-level rankers at a pace of once a month!

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.720
There are many seasoned world champions out there,

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:21.220
and plenty of matches that only last for a short period also exist overseas.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.640
Ah, geez!

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.290
Stop arguing with me just for the sake of arguing!

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:29.820
Actually, I've also been doing some undercover investigation regarding Hayase Tsubasa.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:30.700
Captain!

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.520
I found this on the upper floors of the last match.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.320
A thorn?

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:40.050
It's exceedingly small, but this thorn gives off a Digimon signal.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:42.840
See, look!

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.160
No! He's...!

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:45.700
Stop!

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.790
Let's investigate to find what this is really about.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:51.870
Okay?

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:52.370
Fine.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:24.210
Who are you?

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:27.380
Tohma H. Norstein. I'm a big fan of yours.

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:29.410
Do you mind if I run with you?

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:33.060
No, but I'm not going to lessen my pace for you.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.880
Then let's make a bet.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:40.940
If I'm able to keep up until the end, I'd like to ask you a few questions.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.000
Sure!

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:51.480
We had a bet, didn't we?

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:53.260
Ask me whatever you want.

00:03:56.740 --> 00:03:58.480
Very well.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:04.530
Four years ago, in your match against Uehara Kouichi that decided who entered the world championships...

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:14.460
In that match, Uehara repeatedly made foul plays against you, which threatened your life as a boxer.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:19.890
Damn it, what the hell is that ref looking at?

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:22.210
Uehara's trying to kill you!

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:25.680
You don't have to fight honestly against that guy! You should also...!

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.160
Coach.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.280
I love boxing.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:34.920
I don't ever want to do something that'll dirty the boxing I love.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:41.420
With a strong conviction, you persisted in keeping a clean fight and won.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:42.620
But...

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.370
In exchange for your victory, your right elbow suffered much damage,

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:50.280
and it was even rumored that you were forced to retire for a while.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:57.250
You must have gone through a lot of hardships to make a comeback.

00:04:58.070 --> 00:04:59.460
What would you know?

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:05.090
In that match, I lost many things.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:08.670
The destructive energy of my right hand, and the world championships before my own eyes...

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:11.990
It's true that I felt utterly defeated.

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:13.160
But...

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:18.510
With support from my family and everyone around me, I was able to overcome that hellish rehabilitation...

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:21.240
and I was finally able to make it back to the world championships.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:23.570
I'd rather not listen to your sympathies. As if you understand.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:30.130
Then here's my last question.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:33.790
In the match where you made your comeback, was there anything you thought was strange?

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.350
Was there?

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.580
N-No... Nothing in particular.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:43.050
I see.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:46.680
Well then, I'm looking forward to your title match.

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:59.620
Tohma's Dishonorable Battle

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:59.620
The Secretly Maneuvering Togemon

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.400
Tohma's Dishonorable Battle!

00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.630
The Secretly Maneuvering Togemon!

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:07.720
Amazing, Hayase Tsubasa!

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:10.420
This is his twelfth consecutive victory since his debut!

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:13.150
Here's a playback of the K.O. scene!

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.600
This is...

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:40.160
These wimps don't even count as a warm-up.

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:41.440
C'mon.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.540
Fight me, Hayase-san.

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:46.520
Are you planning to take over the gym?

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:47.840
You could say that.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:50.390
Too bad I don't have time to waste fighting you.

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:52.010
What, you scared?

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:52.690
Hey!

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:57.220
Don't get cocky just because you won against the trainees.

00:07:57.630 --> 00:07:59.340
Who the hell are you?

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:03.420
It's courtesy to name yourself first!

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:06.190
Da... Daimon Masaru.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:09.550
I'm Shiraki, Hayase's coach.

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:13.030
That body that brought him all the way to the world championships must always be treated with care!

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:17.070
I'm not gonna stand by and watch a scoundrel like you try to harm him!

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:18.090
What?!

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:21.180
I'll do anything for him.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:25.320
Breaking two or three bones in your arms is no trouble for me!

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:36.310
Well, that's the sort of readiness a coach needs to train a world champion boxer.

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:38.800
You seem like a decent guy.

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:42.060
I don't mind lookin' after you here in the gym.

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:47.550
Mom, hurry up!

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:49.690
Excuse me!

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:53.870
A magazine reporter?

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:54.580
Yes.

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:56.990
We're doing a feature on the supportive wives of professional players,

00:08:56.990 --> 00:09:00.330
and we're very eager to hear what you have to say as Hayase-senshu's wife.

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:08.140
Starting off, what's the most difficult thing you face as a boxer's wife?

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:12.800
When a match gets closer... he changes.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:17.390
I don't mean the way he talks or his personality.

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:19.430
Somehow, the atmosphere around him changes.

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:23.890
Whenever that happens, it makes me feel nervous as well.

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:28.350
Then, what do you wish for the most?

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:31.790
I want him to come back to us safely.

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:38.110
Of course, it's natural to think so during a match... but it's what I desire the most.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:45.940
I'm sure Manami agrees with me.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.960
Right, Manami?

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:57.590
So, among these three that we've narrowed down, who do you think is the most likely?

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:01.190
I think his coach is suspicious.

00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:02.580
Yeah.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:05.220
Even his face looks evil.

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:09.950
I don't think a nice woman like Mrs. Hayase will do anything bad.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:11.190
That's right.

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:14.610
Tohma, what about you?

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:17.310
I can't declare anything yet.

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:19.070
What the hell!

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:21.830
It's still too early to decide on the criminal.

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:24.610
Something's troubling me...

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:25.880
Captain!

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:29.210
I'd like to reconsider Hayase's surroundings once more!

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:29.830
Excuse me!

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:36.000
Man, he puts on too much airs!

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:59.030
Hayase VS Mwanchai

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:59.030
This weekend begins the world flyweight title matches.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:02.950
The contender Tanonmas Mwanchai has just arrived in Japan.

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:21.130
That's it!

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:28.310
Hey, Tohma-kun!

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:30.140
Hayase-san.

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:34.680
Excuse me for being impolite, but would you mind sparring with me?

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.280
Three rounds of Triple Crown boxing, got it?

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:42.910
Yes.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:44.030
Start the match.

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:47.490
This is the fastest way to make certain.

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:52.050
This punch will be a serious one.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:05.340
'Lo!

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:11.560
Hey, that's Tohma!

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:14.760
What's wrong?

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:16.270
We still have two more rounds.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:19.960
No, there's no longer a need for that.

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:22.680
Thank you for acquiescing to my request.

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:26.250
Yo, Tohma.

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:30.660
Huh? What's with him?

00:12:39.470 --> 00:12:40.910
The match is tomorrow.

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:43.300
I still haven't spotted any abnormal movements yet.

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:51.640
Master.

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:55.490
Why have you become so ill-tempered during this mission?

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.820
I haven't.

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:00.690
But you're acting different from usual.

00:13:06.020 --> 00:13:09.180
I admired Hayase-senshu.

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:15.680
I always wanted to become a clean and strong fighter like him.

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:23.730
His type of boxing was truly my ideal...

00:13:24.590 --> 00:13:26.010
Before he was injured, that is.

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:29.670
Then... he's now different after he was injured?

00:13:30.270 --> 00:13:33.240
That's why you asked for a sparring match to confirm that...

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:36.820
Master, you already know who it is, don't you?

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:38.690
Who is the culprit?

00:14:03.890 --> 00:14:05.660
What the hell are you doing there?!

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:08.460
...Huh?

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:09.420
You, huh?

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:10.720
Don't surprise me.

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:12.800
What are you doing?

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:14.490
What's it look like?

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:18.940
I was thinking, since it's the day before the match, I should enjoy myself a little...

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:21.850
What the hell... That's so misleading.

00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:29.480
It's Hayase.

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:29.900
Shh!

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:50.140
Hayase! What are you doing?

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:50.930
H-Hey!

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:53.500
Coach!

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:56.250
I wanted to go over the combinations again.

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:58.110
Could you help me?

00:14:58.110 --> 00:14:59.430
Sure, that's easy.

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:05.440
This one's struck out, too.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:07.260
What's going on?

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:13.360
Hello?

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:15.110
Honey, we have trouble!

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:45.020
You've finally shown yourself, Togemon!

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:54.990
Togemon

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:54.990
Adult Level

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:46.930
Togemon.

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:51.030
A big cactus with boxing gloves, this Digimon is at the Adult Level.

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:54.990
Its special attack is Chiku-Chiku Bang Bang, which can spray a lot of thorns at once.

00:15:56.310 --> 00:16:01.500
With those thorns all over your body, you can cause a variety of body disorders.

00:16:02.300 --> 00:16:05.120
The previous 7 opponents against Hayase-senshu...

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:08.170
all ended up with unknown physical conditions!

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:11.200
Thanks to those thorns, I expect.

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:15.860
I always had my doubts when I asked myself this:

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:23.100
Would Hayase-senshu, and those who had seen his matches before he was wounded, perform acts of the injustice that he hated?

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:25.230
The answer is, no!

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:29.220
I confirmed that when I fought glove to glove with Hayase-senshu.

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:33.760
Although it didn't have the strength it had years ago, nothing in his heart has changed!

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:42.350
That means, the criminal had never seen any of his matches before he was injured, and yet adored Hayase-senshu dearly...

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:43.000
Yes!

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:45.210
Hayase Manami.

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:49.170
I won't forgive whoever hurts my dad.

00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:53.670
I won't forgive whoever hurts my dad!

00:16:54.350 --> 00:16:55.340
Here it comes, Gaomon!

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:56.940
Spray!

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:11.860
You can't escape!

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:15.740
We just said you're not getting away!

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:17.950
Turn yourself in!

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:19.750
Togemon, jump up!

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:22.660
Oh no!

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:25.170
Togemon, there!

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:52.690
Togemon! Get up on the ring!

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.080
Masaru, aren't you coming?

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:01.770
Wait.

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:05.280
Let's leave this to Gaomon and Tohma.

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:06.410
What are you talking about?

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:10.810
Once you're on the ring, it's strictly one-on-one.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:12.380
That shows what a man's about!

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:23.720
Gao Rush!

00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:36.480
There, Gaomon!

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:37.580
Yes, Master!

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:43.440
The boxing that Master loves...

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:47.630
The pureness of that boxing...

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:51.510
I won't forgive whoever soils that!

00:18:55.210 --> 00:19:00.700
<b>mou nani mo nai sekai ja kandou dekinai</b>

00:18:55.210 --> 00:19:00.700
<b>A world that's full of nothing can't inspire anyone</b>

00:18:56.250 --> 00:18:57.970
A high-rise upper!

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.340
All right!

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:05.660
<b>sou, kizuita sono hi kara wakaru no sa</b>

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:05.660
<b>You'll understand what I mean after the day you realize that</b>

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.770
<b>furue wo tomete</b>

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.770
<b>Stop your trembling</b>

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:11.390
<b>hitomi wo hirake</b>

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:11.390
<b>Open your eyes</b>

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:16.200
<b>kimi no jikan wo tokihanate!</b>

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:16.200
<b>And liberate your time!</b>

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:14.880
Gaomon, time to evolve!

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:16.480
Yes, Master!

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:20.400
<b>mirai e Shootin' star!</b>

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:20.400
<b>Oh shootin' star to the future!</b>

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:22.570
Digisoul Charge!

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:23.690
<b>hikari no aachi egake</b>

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:23.690
<b>Draw an arch of light</b>

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:28.960
<b>todoku no sa shinjitsuzukeru naraba</b>

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:28.960
<b>As long as you keep believing, it'll reach up there</b>

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:27.100
Gaomon, evolve!

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:34.760
<b>kimi wo yobu koe ga kokoro de hajiketara</b>

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:34.760
<b>When the voice that calls you bellows with the heart</b>

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.260
Gaogamon!

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:40.930
<b>subete ga hajimaru Believer!</b>

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:40.930
<b>That's when everything will begin, Believer!</b>

00:19:39.060 --> 00:19:40.810
Spiral Blow!

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:52.190
He did it!

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:58.700
Now it's finished.

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:02.040
I see.

00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:07.050
Manami went that far to ensure that I won...

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:14.760
Hayase-san, won't you please forfeit the title match?

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:16.730
That, I can't do.

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:19.080
But if you fight in your condition...

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:19.800
I know.

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:24.960
Tomorrow may end up being my last match.

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:28.180
But, there's still something I have left to do.

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:35.100
I want to show my daughter how I look as I fight fair-and-square.

